  ],
  "description": "Circuit approximation of the engaged Rev C M234. Uses a 1024-stage 3207-family delay, MC33178-family audio amplifiers, a buffered TL062-family RC relaxation oscillator, transistor input/output filters and ganged low cut. The pot-board high cut and portions of the wet/dry interconnect are reconstructed to the manufacturer control response. The clock and modulation excursion use a fitted period law, and the BBD taps are combined at the centered balance setting. Thru Connected selects wet-only at the main output. A buffered dry Thru is available as a separate schematic node. Supply protection, footswitch muting and clock feedthrough are omitted.",
  "io": {
    "groundNode": "0",
    "inputNode": "in",
    "outputNode": "out"
  },
  "layout": {
    "pots": [
      "Low",
      "High",
      "Level",
      "Rate",
      "Depth"
    ],
    "switches": [
      "Thru Connected"
    ]
  },
  "name": "MXR M234 Analog Chorus",
  "version": 3,
